Why the list is not updated
---------------------------
1. Your +page.svelte receives its `notes` array from the `load` function in +page.server.js.
2. When you submit the *delete* form with `use:enhance`, SvelteKit turns the request into a `fetch` instead of a full page navigation.
3. SvelteKit therefore **does not automatically re-run the `load` function**. The JSON returned by the action is merged into the `form` store only; the original `data` object (which contains the notes) is left untouched. The component keeps rendering the stale `notes` it already has.

How to make the UI refresh — 3 common approaches
-----------------------------------------------
A. Invalidate the page after the action (recommended)
```svelte
<!-- +page.svelte -->
<script>
  import { enhance } from "$app/forms";
  import { invalidateAll } from "$app/navigation";

  // When the action finishes successfully, invalidate all data
  const enhanceDelete = enhance({
    after() {
      invalidateAll(); // will rerun this page's load and re-fetch notes
    }
  });
</script>

{#each data.notes as note (note.id)}
  <form action="?/delete" method="post" use:enhance={enhanceDelete}>
    <input type="hidden" name="id" value={note.id} />
    <button aria-label="delete {note.title}">🗑️</button>
  </form>
{/each}
```
```js
// +page.server.js
export const actions = {
  delete: async ({ request, locals }) => {
    const { id } = Object.fromEntries(await request.formData());
    await locals.db.note.delete({ where: { id } });
    return { success: true };
  }
};

export const load = async ({ locals }) => {
  return { notes: await locals.db.note.findMany({ orderBy: { createdAt: "desc" } }) };
};
```

B. Return the new list from the action and read it from the `form` store
```js
// +page.server.js (action only)
return { updated: await locals.db.note.findMany() };
```
```svelte
<script>
  import { form } from "$app/forms";
  export let data;

  // reactively switch to the list returned by the action if present
  $: notes = $form?.updated ?? data.notes;
</script>
```

C. Skip progressive enhancement (quick-and-dirty)
Remove `use:enhance`, let the browser perform a normal POST. The page will fully reload and `load()` will naturally run again.

Common pitfalls / reminders
---------------------------
