Below is one complete fix. It relies on native HTML5 validation for title and a small custom check for the optional description field so that end-users see standard error bubbles and the form never reaches fn.popupActionHandler.submit() unless the data are valid.

<!-- ①  Cleaned-up HTML  -->
<form id="editFormPhoto" method="post" accept-charset="UTF-8"><!-- removed action="javascript:…" because it suppresses native validation -->
  <input name="p"  type="hidden" value="photo" />
  <input name="a"  type="hidden" value="editPhoto" />
  <input name="id" type="hidden" />

  <div class="formGroup">
    <label class="text-black-title" for="photoTitle"><b class="req">*</b> Title:</label>
    <input id="photoTitle" name="title" minlength="1" maxlength="100" required
           type="text" class="formControl border-radius-6"
           placeholder="Enter a title (1–100 characters)" />
  </div>

  <div class="formGroup">
    <label class="text-black-title" for="photoDesc">Description:</label>
    <textarea id="photoDesc" name="desc" maxlength="5000"
              class="formControl border-radius-6"
              placeholder="Up to 5 000 characters"></textarea>
  </div>

  <div class="modal-footer modal-body-padding">
    <button type="button" class="btn" data-bs-dismiss="modal">Cancel</button>
    <input id="btnSubmit" type="submit" class="btn btn-default border-radius-20" value="Save changes" />
  </div>
</form>

<!-- ②  JavaScript validation shim  -->
<script>
(function () {
  const form  = document.getElementById('editFormPhoto');
  const title = form.elements['title'];
  const desc  = form.elements['desc'];

  form.addEventListener('submit', function (e) {
    // Let the browser run built-in checks first
    if (!form.checkValidity()) {
      // If built-in constraints fail the browser will still show bubbles,
      // but we block the scripted submit below.
      e.preventDefault();
      e.stopPropagation();
      return;
    }

    // Extra manual check: description length (browser already enforces "maxlength",
    // but this shows a friendlier alert in case JS manipulates it later)
    if (desc.value.trim().length > 5000) {
      alert('Description may not exceed 5,000 characters.');
      e.preventDefault();
      return;
    }

    /* All good → call existing AJAX helper and prevent native post */
    e.preventDefault();
    fn.popupActionHandler.submit('editFormPhoto');
  });
})();
</script>

WHY THIS FIX WORKS
1. Removing the “javascript:” pseudo-URL from the action attribute allows the browser’s native constraint validation API (minlength, maxlength, required) to run. When the protocol was “javascript:”, the form never performed default submission, so the validity check that precedes it was skipped.
2. Attaching a submit listener lets us prevent the default submission, run additional JS checks or AJAX submission, and only invoke fn.popupActionHandler.submit() when the form is valid.
3. Using required on the title ensures that an empty string still triggers the minlength bubble instead of silently passing as an optional field.
4. Edge cases are handled: we trim whitespace, titles of exactly 1 or 100 characters pass, UTF-8 multibyte characters count as single characters because the browser’s length property uses UTF-16 code units.
5. By leaving Bootstrap modal markup untouched, the modal opens/closes exactly as before.

